# svrnty self-host — environment template.
# For Docker self-host (recommended): copy to `.env` (gitignored), fill in, then run
#   `docker compose up -d --build`.  For a direct `next start` run instead: copy to `.env.local`.
# NEVER commit real secrets. Full guide: docs/SELF_HOSTING.md.

# ── Domain: the one knob that makes a self-hosted instance YOURS ──────────────
# Your bare domain (no scheme). Every share link (/c/<code>), claimed-slug URL, and
# display string points here. Default is the managed nursery svrnty.is — a DEFAULT,
# not a dependency ("the tree in the seed"): a self-certifying durable_id needs no
# permission from svrnty.is to relocate. See src/lib/config/domain.ts.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SVRNTY_DOMAIN=svrnty.is

# Optional: override the scheme+host explicitly. Defaults to https://$NEXT_PUBLIC_SVRNTY_DOMAIN.
# Set this for http / localhost during development.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SVRNTY_BASE_URL=https://svrnty.is

# ── Satellite (runs by default; the `registration` service) ──────────────────
# REQUIRED. The satellite refuses to start without it, and `docker compose up` stops with
# an error until it's set. A server-side bearer secret for the satellite's maintenance
# routes: never a NEXT_PUBLIC_ var, never shared. Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
SATELLITE_ADMIN_KEY=
#
# Optional. Who may tell the satellite the real client address (X-Forwarded-For). The app
# is the only hop in front of it, so the default "app" is right for this compose file.
# SATELLITE_TRUSTED_PROXY_NAMES=app

# ── Satellite address + image (rarely needed) ─────────────────────────────────
# Compose points the app at the satellite for you. Keep the service host as "registration":
# one slug route hardcodes it.
# SATELLITE_URL=http://registration:8101
#
# Use a prebuilt satellite image instead of building infra/svrnty.
# REGISTRATION_IMAGE=svrnty-registration:latest

# Set to on to show the "not live yet" notice on the home page. Anything else, or unset, is off.
# Read at runtime, so a restart changes it; no rebuild.
# SVRNTY_NOT_LIVE_BANNER=off
